[I] Library of routines for managing a database

[T] Kyoto Cabinet is a library of routines for managing a database, a
[T] straightforward implementation of DBM by Mikio Hirabayashi and successor
[T] of Tokyo Cabinet. Each record is a key-value pair stored in hash or B+
[T] tree files or in memory, with very fast access and support for
[T] transactions and multi-threading.

[U] https://dbmx.net/kyotocabinet/

[A] Kyotocabinet Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

